{
  "schema": 1,
  "goals": [
    "Say how old you are and ask someone's age",
    "Conjugate avoir and venir in the present tense",
    "Count to 69",
    "Say where you're from and what nationality you are",
    "Say where you live and which languages you speak"
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "fr-1.2-1",
      "title": "J'ai quatorze ans",
      "subtitle": "The verb avoir and age",
      "topics": ["avoir", "age"],
      "words": ["verbs-irregular#to have", "countries#age", "countries#how old are you?", "time#year"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "The verb avoir (to have)", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "*Avoir* (to have) is, together with *être*, the most important French verb. It's irregular, so learn it by heart."},
          {"type": "table", "verb": "avoir", "tense": "present"},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Shortening", "en": "Before *ai*, *je* shortens: *j'ai* (I have), never *je ai*."},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "J'ai un frère.", "en": "I have a brother."},
            {"fr": "Tu as un chien ?", "en": "Do you have a dog? (tu)"},
            {"fr": "Nous avons un chat.", "en": "We have a cat."},
            {"fr": "Ils ont une maison.", "en": "They have a house."}
          ]},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Nous ___ un chat.", "a": ["avons"], "hint": "avoir"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "How old are you? (tu)", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "Watch out: in French you don't give your age with *être* but with *avoir*. You literally say \"I have 14 years\": *J'ai quatorze ans.*"},
          {"type": "table", "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["How old are you? (tu)", "Quel âge as-tu ? / Tu as quel âge ?"],
            ["How old are you? (formal)", "Quel âge avez-vous ?"],
            ["How old is he?", "Quel âge a-t-il ? / Il a quel âge ?"],
            ["I'm 14.", "J'ai quatorze ans."]
          ]},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Don't forget ans", "en": "You can't leave out *ans* (years): *J'ai quatorze ans*, not just *J'ai quatorze*. Only for one year is it singular: *J'ai un an.*"},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Why a-t-il?", "en": "In the question *a-t-il ?* a *-t-* goes between the two vowels so that it's easy to say."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "build", "en": "I'm fourteen.", "a": ["J'ai quatorze ans."]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-f", "type": "form", "verb": "avoir", "tense": "present"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "J'___ quinze ans.", "a": ["ai"], "hint": "avoir"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Tu ___ quel âge ?", "a": ["as"], "hint": "avoir"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Paul ___ seize ans.", "a": ["a"], "hint": "avoir"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Vous ___ un chien ?", "a": ["avez"], "hint": "avoir"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elles ___ douze ans.", "a": ["ont"], "hint": "avoir"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-06", "type": "build", "en": "I'm fourteen.", "a": ["J'ai quatorze ans."], "why": "Age is given with the verb avoir and the word ans."},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-07", "type": "build", "en": "How old are you? (tu)", "a": ["{Quel âge as-tu|Tu as quel âge|Quel âge est-ce que tu as} ?"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-08", "type": "build", "en": "He's twelve.", "a": ["Il a douze ans."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-09", "type": "build", "en": "How old are you, madam?", "a": ["{Quel âge avez-vous|Vous avez quel âge}, madame ?"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-10", "type": "build", "en": "I have a brother and a sister.", "a": ["J'ai un frère et une sœur."], "hint": "brother = un frère, sister = une sœur"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-11", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it formal (vous)", "fr": "Quel âge as-tu ?", "a": ["{Quel âge avez-vous|Vous avez quel âge} ?"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-12", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Change the person to nous", "fr": "J'ai un chat.", "a": ["{Nous avons|On a} un chat."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-13", "type": "order", "en": "Léa is ten.", "a": ["Léa a dix ans"], "extra": ["est", "as"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-1-14", "type": "build", "en": "I'm fifteen and I'm Czech.", "a": ["J'ai quinze ans et je suis tchèque."]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-1.2-2",
      "title": "Les nombres jusqu'à 69",
      "subtitle": "Numbers 20 to 69",
      "topics": ["numbers"],
      "words": ["numbers#twenty-one", "numbers#twenty-two", "numbers#thirty", "numbers#thirty-one", "numbers#forty", "numbers#fifty", "numbers#sixty"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "The tens", "blocks": [
          {"type": "table", "textCols": [0], "rows": [["20", "vingt"], ["30", "trente"], ["40", "quarante"], ["50", "cinquante"], ["60", "soixante"]]},
          {"type": "text", "en": "The other numbers are made of a ten and a unit, joined by a **hyphen**: *vingt-deux* (22), *trente-cinq* (35), *quarante-huit* (48)."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "trente, quarante, ___, soixante", "a": ["cinquante"]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Watch out for one", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "When a number ends in one, you put *et* between the ten and the unit and leave out the hyphen: *vingt et un* (21), *trente et un* (31), *quarante et un* (41), *cinquante et un* (51), *soixante et un* (61)."},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "New spelling", "en": "Since the 1990 spelling reform you may use hyphens everywhere: *vingt-et-un*. Both are correct."},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "vingt-trois", "en": "23"},
            {"fr": "trente-quatre", "en": "34"},
            {"fr": "quarante-cinq", "en": "45"},
            {"fr": "cinquante et un", "en": "51"},
            {"fr": "soixante-huit", "en": "68"}
          ]},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "trente-neuf, quarante, ___", "a": ["quarante et un", "quarante-et-un"]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Phone numbers", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "The French read phone numbers **in pairs**: 06 12 34 56 → *zéro six, douze, trente-quatre, cinquante-six*."},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "Mon numéro, c'est le zéro six, vingt-deux, trente et un, quarante-cinq.", "en": "My number is 06 22 31 45."}
          ]}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "vingt, vingt et un, ___", "a": ["vingt-deux"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "J'ai ___ ans.", "a": ["vingt-cinq"], "hint": "25"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Il a ___ ans.", "a": ["quarante et un", "quarante-et-un"], "hint": "41"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elle a ___ ans.", "a": ["trente-huit"], "hint": "38"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Madame Dubois a ___ ans.", "a": ["cinquante-deux"], "hint": "52"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Monsieur Martin a ___ ans.", "a": ["soixante-sept"], "hint": "67"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-07", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Dix et dix font ___.", "a": ["vingt"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-08", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Vingt et vingt font ___.", "a": ["quarante"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-09", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Trente et trente font ___.", "a": ["soixante"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-10", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Vingt-cinq et vingt-cinq font ___.", "a": ["cinquante"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-11", "type": "build", "en": "I'm twenty-one.", "a": ["J'ai {vingt et un|vingt-et-un} ans."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-12", "type": "build", "en": "Paul is thirty-six.", "a": ["Paul a trente-six ans."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-2-13", "type": "build", "en": "Forty and twenty make sixty.", "a": ["Quarante et vingt font soixante."]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-1.2-3",
      "title": "Pays et nationalités",
      "subtitle": "Countries and nationalities",
      "topics": ["nationalities"],
      "words": ["countries#France", "countries#the Czech Republic, Czechia", "countries#Slovakia", "countries#Germany", "countries#England", "countries#Spain", "countries#Italy", "countries#the United States", "countries#Slovak (nationality)", "countries#German (man)", "countries#German (woman)", "countries#English (man)", "countries#English (woman)", "countries#Spanish (man)", "countries#Spanish (woman)", "countries#Italian (man)", "countries#Italian (woman)", "countries#American (man)", "countries#American (woman)"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "Countries", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "In French, country names take an **article**. Countries ending in *-e* are mostly feminine: *la France, la Slovaquie, l'Allemagne, l'Italie*. The others are masculine: *le Canada, le Portugal*. Some are plural: *les États-Unis*."},
          {"type": "table", "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["the Czech Republic", "la République tchèque / la Tchéquie"],
            ["Slovakia", "la Slovaquie"],
            ["France", "la France"],
            ["Germany", "l'Allemagne"],
            ["Austria", "l'Autriche"],
            ["England", "l'Angleterre"],
            ["Spain", "l'Espagne"],
            ["Italy", "l'Italie"],
            ["Canada", "le Canada"],
            ["the USA", "les États-Unis"]
          ]},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Exception", "en": "*Le Mexique* ends in *-e* but is masculine."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "C'est ___ Canada.", "a": ["le"], "hint": "article"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Nationality", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "A nationality has a masculine and a feminine form. Usually you add *-e* to the masculine: *allemand → allemande, anglais → anglaise, espagnol → espagnole, américain → américaine, français → française*."},
          {"type": "text", "en": "Some forms change more: *italien → italienne, autrichien → autrichienne, canadien → canadienne*. Nationalities that already end in *-e* don't change: *tchèque, slovaque, belge, suisse*."},
          {"type": "table", "head": ["man", "woman"], "rows": [
            ["français", "française"], ["allemand", "allemande"], ["anglais", "anglaise"], ["espagnol", "espagnole"],
            ["américain", "américaine"], ["italien", "italienne"], ["tchèque", "tchèque"], ["slovaque", "slovaque"]
          ]},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Small or capital letter?", "en": "When a nationality describes a person, it takes a small letter: *Il est allemand.* When it's a noun (a German), it takes a capital: *un Allemand, une Allemande*."},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Pronunciation", "en": "In the masculine the final consonant is silent (*allemand* [almɑ̃]), in the feminine it is pronounced (*allemande* [almɑ̃d])."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Marie est ___.", "a": ["allemande"], "hint": "German (woman)"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "C'est ___ France.", "a": ["la"], "hint": "article"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ce sont ___ États-Unis.", "a": ["les"], "hint": "article"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Paul est anglais et Kate est ___.", "a": ["anglaise"], "hint": "English (woman)"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Marco est ___.", "a": ["italien"], "hint": "Italian (man)"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Giulia est ___.", "a": ["italienne"], "hint": "Italian (woman)"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Juan et Pablo sont ___.", "a": ["espagnols"], "hint": "Spanish (men)"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-07", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Lena et Anna sont ___.", "a": ["allemandes"], "hint": "German (women)"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-08", "type": "build", "en": "I'm Slovak.", "a": ["Je suis slovaque."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-09", "type": "build", "en": "She's American.", "a": ["Elle est américaine."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-10", "type": "build", "en": "They're German.", "a": ["Ils sont allemands."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-11", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est espagnol.", "a": ["Elle est espagnole."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-12", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est italien.", "a": ["Elle est italienne."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-13", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est tchèque.", "a": ["Elle est tchèque."], "why": "Tchèque ends in -e, so it doesn't change in the feminine."},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-14", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it plural", "fr": "Il est américain.", "a": ["Ils sont américains."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-3-15", "type": "order", "en": "I'm Czech and she's French.", "a": ["Je suis tchèque et elle est française"], "extra": ["français", "il"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-1.2-4",
      "title": "J'habite à Prague",
      "subtitle": "Home, origin and languages",
      "topics": ["places-prep", "venir"],
      "words": ["verbs-irregular#to come", "verbs#to live", "basics#I live", "basics#where", "basics#where from", "countries#where do you live?", "countries#where are you from?", "countries#country", "countries#language", "countries#Czech (language)", "countries#German (language)", "countries#Spanish (language)", "school#French (language)", "school#English (language)", "geography#Prague", "geography#Paris"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "Where do you live?", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "With **towns** you use *à*: *J'habite à Prague.* (I live in Prague.) With **countries** it depends on the gender: feminine → *en*, masculine → *au*, plural → *aux*."},
          {"type": "table", "head": ["", "preposition", "example"], "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["town", "à", "à Prague, à Paris"],
            ["feminine country", "en", "en France, en Italie"],
            ["masculine country", "au", "au Canada, au Portugal"],
            ["plural", "aux", "aux États-Unis"]
          ]},
          {"type": "text", "en": "The verb *habiter* (to live) is regular:"},
          {"type": "table", "verb": "habiter", "tense": "present"},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "J'habite ___ Prague.", "a": ["à"]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Where are you from?", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "*Venir de* means \"to come from\". The verb *venir* is irregular."},
          {"type": "table", "verb": "venir", "tense": "present"},
          {"type": "text", "en": "Before a town or a feminine country *de* is enough (*d'* before a vowel): *Je viens de Prague. Je viens de France. Je viens d'Italie.* With masculine countries it's *du*, in the plural *des*: *Il vient du Canada. Elle vient des États-Unis.*"},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "D'où viens-tu ? Je viens de Prague.", "en": "Where are you from? I'm from Prague."},
            {"fr": "Marco vient d'Italie.", "en": "Marco is from Italy."},
            {"fr": "Nous venons du Canada.", "en": "We're from Canada."}
          ]},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Il vient ___ Canada.", "a": ["du"]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Languages", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "A language has the same form as the masculine nationality and takes a small letter: *le français, l'anglais, l'allemand, le tchèque*. After *parler* the article is usually left out: *Je parle français.*"},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "Je parle tchèque, anglais et un peu français.", "en": "I speak Czech, English and a little French."},
            {"fr": "Tu parles allemand ?", "en": "Do you speak German? (tu)"},
            {"fr": "Au Canada, on parle anglais et français.", "en": "In Canada they speak English and French."}
          ]},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "on = people", "en": "*On parle* means \"people speak\" or \"is spoken\". Here *on* means people in general."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "build", "en": "I speak Czech and English.", "a": ["Je parle {|le }tchèque et {|l'}anglais."]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-f", "type": "form", "verb": "venir", "tense": "present"},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "J'habite ___ Paris.", "a": ["à"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Nous habitons ___ France.", "a": ["en"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ils habitent ___ Canada.", "a": ["au"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elle habite ___ États-Unis.", "a": ["aux"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Je viens ___ Prague.", "a": ["de"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Tu viens ___Italie ?", "a": ["d'"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-07", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Paul vient ___ Canada.", "a": ["du"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-08", "type": "build", "en": "I live in Prague.", "a": ["J'habite à Prague."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-09", "type": "build", "en": "Where do you live?", "a": ["{Où habites-tu|Tu habites où|Où est-ce que tu habites} ?"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-10", "type": "build", "en": "Where are you from? I'm from Prague.", "a": ["{D'où viens-tu|Tu viens d'où|D'où es-tu} ? Je viens de Prague."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-11", "type": "build", "en": "We live in the Czech Republic.", "a": ["{Nous habitons|On habite} en {République tchèque|Tchéquie}."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-12", "type": "build", "en": "Do you speak French? (tu)", "a": ["{Tu parles|Parles-tu|Est-ce que tu parles} {|le }français ?"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-13", "type": "build", "en": "I'm from Germany, but I live in France.", "a": ["Je viens d'Allemagne, mais j'habite en France."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-14", "type": "order", "en": "In Canada they speak French.", "a": ["Au Canada on parle français"], "extra": ["en", "parlons"]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-15", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Change the person to nous", "fr": "Je viens de Prague.", "a": ["{Nous venons|On vient} de Prague."]},
        {"id": "fr-1.2-4-16", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Change the person to ils", "fr": "Il vient d'Espagne.", "a": ["Ils viennent d'Espagne."]}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "test": {
    "pass": 0.7,
    "count": 20,
    "words": 6,
    "pool": [
